   "source": [
    "# Task 2.1: A Century of Football — Performance Intelligence Report\n",
    "\n",
    "## 1. Introduction\n",
    "This report analyzes 150 years of international football (1872–2026) using three \n",
    "merged datasets — `results.csv`, `goalscorers.csv`, and `shootouts.csv` — to answer \n",
    "key questions about historical team dominance, efficiency, drama, collapses, and the \n",
    "evolution of the game across eras.\n",
    "\n",
    "## 2. Data Cleaning & Preparation\n",
    "The `results.csv` dataset contains 49,520 matches spanning 1872–2026. During initial \n",
    "exploration, 2 rows with missing scores were found (the 2026 World Cup bronze final \n",
    "and the final). Since we had already watched these two matches, the actual results \n",
    "were manually verified and imputed (France 4–6 England; Spain 1–0 Argentina after \n",
    "extra time) rather than dropping the rows.\n",
    "\n",
    "The `date` column was converted to datetime, and `year`/`decade` features were \n",
    "engineered for time-based analysis.\n",
    "\n",
    "A significant data quality issue was discovered when examining team names: the dataset \n",
    "contains 337 unique team entries, nearly 60% more than FIFA's 211 official member \n",
    "associations. Investigation revealed these extra entries include defunct historical \n",
    "states (Yugoslavia, Czechoslovakia), disputed/unrecognized territories (Catalonia, \n",
    "Tibet, Kurdistan), and small island entities competing in separate competitions like \n",
    "the Island Games (Jersey, Guernsey, Alderney) — none of which are comparable to FIFA \n",
    "member nations for performance benchmarking. A curated exclusion list was built to \n",
    "filter these ~128 entities out of team-level analyses.\n",
    "\n",
    "Separately, `goalscorers.csv` required its own cleaning: 936 own-goal entries were \n",
    "excluded (as they should not count toward a player's individual scoring tally), along \n",
    "with 44 rows with missing scorer names, all traced to a single under-documented 1980 \n",
    "Pacific tournament.\n",
    "\n",
    "To enable team-level analysis, `results.csv` was reshaped from a match-per-row format \n",
    "into a team-per-row format (99,040 rows — exactly double the match count), allowing \n",
    "every team's home and away performances to be aggregated together.\n",
    "\n",
    "## 3. Top Performers\n",
    "\n",
    "### 3.1 Top Scoring Teams (FIFA members only)\n",
    "England (2,401 goals), Germany (2,331), and Brazil (2,315) lead all-time goal totals. \n",
    "However, this ranking is heavily influenced by longevity — these teams have simply \n",
    "played the most matches (1,000+) over 150 years, not necessarily the highest scoring \n",
    "rate per match (see Section 4).\n",
    "\n",
    "### 3.2 Top Individual Goalscorers\n",
    "Cristiano Ronaldo (124 goals), Harry Kane (75), and Lionel Messi (71) top the \n",
    "individual scoring charts.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Limitation:** This ranking should be read with caution. Ali Daei (Iran), historically \n",
